Value":0,"awayScore":0,"homeScore":0,"text":"Josh Doan Backhand saved by Jacob Markstrom","type":{"id":"506","text":"Shot","abbreviation":"shot-on-goal"},"clock":{"displayValue":"1:02"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"2"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"4874870","displayName":"Josh Doan","shortName":"J. Doan"},"type":"shooter"},{"athlete":{"id":"5452","displayName":"Jacob Markstrom","shortName":"J. Markstrom"},"type":"saver"}]},{"id":"401892485000000090","scoringPlay":false,"scoreValue":0,"awayScore":0,"homeScore":0,"text":"Goalie Stopped","type":{"id":"516","text":"Stoppage","abbreviation":"stoppage"},"clock":{"displayValue":"1:04"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"}},{"id":"401892485000000630","scoringPlay":false,"scoreValue":0,"awayScore":0,"homeScore":0,"text":"Sam Reinhart faceoff won against Noah Ostlund","type":{"id":"502","text":"Face Off","abbreviation":"faceoff"},"clock":{"displayValue":"1:04"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"26"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"3114722","displayName":"Sam Reinhart","shortName":"S. Reinhart"},"type":"face-off-winner"},{"athlete":{"id":"5080160","displayName":"Noah Ostlund","shortName":"N. Ostlund"}}]}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"1848","fullName":"KeyBank Center","address":{"city":"Buffalo","state":"NY","country":"USA"},"grass":false,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/nhl/day/1848.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day"]}]},"attendance":19070,"officials":[{"fullName":"Eric Furlatt","displayName":"Eric Furlatt","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Carter Sandlak","displayName":"Carter Sandlak","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"James Tobias","displayName":"James Tobias","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Joe Mahon","displayName":"Joe Mahon","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"Noah Ostlund scores go-ahead goal in third period in Sabres' 5-3 win over Panthers","description":"— Noah Ostlund scored the go-ahead goal on the power play 7:15 into the third period, and the Buffalo Sabres defeated the Florida Panthers 5-3 on Monday in an outing both teams lost key players to injury.","story":"BUFFALO, N.Y. -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5080160/noah-ostlund\">Noah Ostlund</a> scored the go-ahead goal on the power play 7:15 into the third period, and the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/buf/buffalo-sabres\">Buffalo Sabres</a> defeated the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/fla/florida-panthers\">Florida Panthers</a> 5-3 on Monday in an outing both teams lost key players to injury.\n\n\r\n              Sabres captain <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4294163/rasmus-dahlin\">Rasmus Dahlin</a> scored his second goal of the season before not returning after <a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/buffalo-sabres-rasmus-dahlin-e5cf3bc9d29b13a448f7c12c49f1b01e\">sustaining an upper-body injury</a> early in the second period. \n\n\r\n              Coach Lindy Ruff listed Dahlin as day to day, while adding the defenseman won't initially join the team in opening a three-game road trip at Montreal on Tuesday.\n\n\r\n              Meantime, Panthers starting goalie <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5452/jacob-markstrom\">Jacob Markstrom</a> did not return after allowing two goals on 11 shots in the first period. He was replaced by <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4587845/akira-schmid\">Akira Schmid</a>, who finished allowing three goals on 21 shots. \n\n\r\n              Coach Paul Maurice said Markstrom felt something tighten, and downplayed the severity by saying: “There's no injury there.”\n\n\r\n              Buffalo also got goals from <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4024988/tage-thompson\">Tage Thompson</a>, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4874870/josh-doan\">Josh Doan</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4378669/ryan-mcleod\">Ryan McLeod</a> in an outing the Sabres never trailed.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4233889/ukko-pekka-luukkonen\">Ukko-Pekka Luukkonen</a> allowed one goal on 14 shots for the win in a backup role. He entered 6:25 into the second period after starter <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4736758/colten-ellis\">Colten Ellis</a> allowed two goals on nine shots. Ellis was pulled after <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3114722/sam-reinhart\">Sam Reinhart</a> tied the game at 2 by poking in a loose puck that dribbled into the crease behind the goalie.\n\n\r\n              Reinhart scored twice and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697395/anton-lundell\">Anton Lundell</a> also had a goal. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4319858/brady-tkachuk\">Brady Tkachuk</a> got his first point with the Panthers as he assisted on Reinhart's second goal.\n\n\r\n              Florida (2-2-2) has dropped two straight following a 4-1 home-opening loss to Minnesota on Saturday.\n\n\r\n              With the game tied at 3, Ostlund scored by tapping in Zach Benson’s pass through the crease. Buffalo converted two of five power-play opportunities after opening the season going 1 of 17.\n\n\r\n              The Panthers converted two of four power-play chances after entering the game 1 of 28.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Panthers: Travel to play Columbus on Tuesday night.\n\n\r\n              Sabres: Follow a five-game homestand to play at Montreal on Tuesday night. ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-10-12T21:18:26Z"}}